  "compatibility": [
    "WebGL2, ES modules, Canvas 2D, Pointer Events. A static photograph remains available without WebGL.",
    "Tested with Chromium and Playwright WebKit. Touch drag and keyboard brushing; reduced motion applies changes without animated rotation.",
    "Up to 12,544 instanced tiles. One shared tile geometry, at most four draw calls, one capped 2048px photograph texture. No per-tile shadow maps.",
    "Local PNG, JPEG and WebP uploads under 12 MB / 24 megapixels. No uploads to a server; presets and source exports retain bundled images."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Real beveled geometry rotates around a central pin; stationary bearing caps show the hinge axis.",
    "Uncover mode rotates tiles up to 90\u00b0 over a separate photograph. Reverse mode maps the image to the back faces and reflects UVs about the hinge to preserve registration at 180\u00b0.",
    "Pointer segments are interpolated analytically. Speed broadens the swept field; nearby tiles turn further and distant tiles react later.",
    "Reveal all always reaches the full image and stays open; Close in a wave resets the surface. The flip-angle control applies to brushing.",
    "Seven materials and six presets. Open photograph demonstrates a complete reveal leading into a content view."
  ],
  "reuse": [
    "Serve the ZIP over local HTTP and open example.html; no installation or build required. Exact Three.js browser runtime included.",
    "Use createSequinSurface from engine.js for an independent image, or mount from index.js for the complete instrument and controls.",
    "The pure TileState model accepts normalized brush segments. Custom image, grid, material, interaction and completion callbacks are independent of the site.",
    "See gallery-demo.html for a gallery transition and README.md for lifecycle, performance, schema and licensing."
  ],
  "comparison": "none"
